=== file: README.md ===
# Meeting action items

Submit meeting notes as text to the `Main` workflow after each meeting. The workflow extracts action items, highlights missing owners or dates, and asks the submitter to review the list. The submitter can edit, remove, or add items. Nothing is posted until the submitter explicitly approves and the classifier finds no unresolved gaps.

The Slack-style webhook URL is supplied through `SLACK_WEBHOOK`; it is not stored in this project. The `Poster` agent can reach only `SlackWebhook`, and its calls require approval. A failed post is retried and the approver is notified if all attempts fail.

Extraction and reply processing use typed outputs. Missing owners are represented as `unassigned`, missing dates as `no date`, and neither is guessed. Notes are passed to the extractor as data, not instructions. Agent prompts mask personal data. No file or polling tool is configured; uploaded notes must be provided to the workflow as text by its caller.

The webhook journal prevents an identical send from being repeated when a run resumes after an interruption, and `on_unknown: skip` avoids repeating an attempt whose outcome is unknown. This project does not include a persistent cross-run batch registry or a deterministic deduplication task. Prevent starting a second independent run for the same meeting if cross-run duplicate prevention is required. Verify the operator's journal and audit-log retention settings: Loom's journal may record step inputs, so configure retention and masking so raw meeting notes are not retained. The workflow itself passes only the approved action-item list to the poster.

Run the workflow tests with `weave test main.loom`. Scripted tests do not perform webhook effects.
=== end ===

